hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24349","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, then he mentioned the hadith, Abu Hurayrah said: So I met Abu Basrah al-Ghifari, who said: From where have you come, so I said: From al-Tur, so he said: Had I met you before you went to it, you would not have gone to it, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Mounts are not saddled except to three mosques: to the Sacred Mosque, and to my mosque, and to the mosque of Iliya, or Bayt al-Maqdis, he doubts."
"24350","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that Abu Basrah went out in Ramadan from Alexandria, his food was brought to him, and it was said to him: Our dwellings have not yet disappeared from us, so he said: Do you turn away from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so we remained breaking the fast until they reached such and such place."
"24351","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that he said: Abu Basrah al-Ghifari met Abu Hurayrah while he was coming from al-Tur, and said: From where have you come, he said: From al-Tur, I prayed in it, he said: Had I met you before you departed to it, you would not have departed, I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Journeys are not undertaken except to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, and this mosque of mine, and al-Masjid al-Aqsa."
"24352","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yazid informed us, Ibn Hubayrah narrated to me, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, that Amr ibn al-As addressed the people on Friday and said: Abu Basrah narrated to me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has added for you a prayer, and it is witr, so pray it between the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer, Abu Tamim said: So Abu Dharr took my hand and walked in the mosque to Abu Basrah, and said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying what Amr said, Abu Basrah said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
